{"task_id": "Mbpp/67", "solution": "def bell_number(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the nth Bell number, representing the number of ways to partition a set of n elements.\n    It builds Bell's triangle to compute the value efficiently.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n\n    # Initialize a 2D array to store Bell's triangle values.\n    # triangle[i][j] stores the j-th number in the i-th row of the triangle.\n    triangle = [[0] * (n + 1) for _ in range(n + 1)]\n\n    # The first element of the 0-th row is 1 (B(0)).\n    triangle[0][0] = 1\n\n    # Build Bell's triangle row by row.\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        # The first element of the current row is the last element of the previous row.\n        triangle[i][0] = triangle[i-1][i-1]\n        for j in range(1, i + 1):\n            # Each subsequent element is the sum of the element to its left\n            # in the same row and the element above it in the previous row.\n            triangle[i][j] = triangle[i][j-1] + triangle[i-1][j-1]\n\n    # The nth Bell number is the first element of the nth row of the triangle.\n    return triangle[n][0]"}
